2026-03-26 19:26:57 - Agent_20260326191704 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed 7 queries covering path traversal vulnerabilities in Spark Java framework's static file resource handlers. 

TRUE POSITIVES (3):
1. ClassPathResourceHandler.getResource() (line 60-84): Missing WEB-INF/META-INF sensitive directory filter - allows HTTP requests for /WEB-INF/web.xml etc. to be served from classpath. Full dataflow confirmed from getServletPath()/getPathInfo() through UriPath.canonical() and ClassPathResource construction with no sensitive path blocking.

2. JarResourceHandler.getResourceStream() (line 78-109): Same missing sensitive directory filter issue - no WEB-INF/META-INF blocking before calling JarResourceHandler.class.getResourceAsStream(path).

3. ExternalResourceHandler.getResource() (line 57-86): Same missing sensitive directory filter - no deny-list for sensitive paths when serving external filesystem resources. UriPath.canonical() handles '../' traversal but no filtering of WEB-INF/sensitive paths.

FALSE POSITIVES (6):
1. ClassPathResource.java line 182 - Protocol prefix injection not exploitable via ClassLoader.getResource() which doesn't interpret URL schemes.
2. AbstractResourceHandler.java lines 106/113 - startsWith(SLASH) checks are path concatenation helpers, not security checks.
3. StaticFilesConfiguration.java line 155 - ClassPathResource construction uses developer-configured server-side value, not user input.
4. MatcherFilter.java line 100 - getRequestURI() flows to route matching only, not to static file serving.
5. ClassPathResourceHandler.java line 61 - startsWith('/') is format validation, not bypassable containment check.
6. ClassPathResourceHandler.java lines 70/74 - Protocol prefix injection not exploitable via ClassLoader.getResource().
